3296" data-end=3D"3345">3. Comment fonctionne le "Lifting State Up" ?</stro=
ng></h2>
<p data-start=3D"3347" data-end=3D"3410" class=3D"">Le processus de lifting=
 state up implique deux grandes =C3=A9tapes :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"3411" data-end=3D"3540">
<li data-start=3D"3411" data-end=3D"3459" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3414" data-end=3D"3459" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
414" data-end=3D"3458">D=C3=A9placer l=E2=80=99=C3=A9tat dans un composant =
parent</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3460" data-end=3D"3540" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3463" data-end=3D"3540" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
463" data-end=3D"3539">Passer cet =C3=A9tat et les fonctions n=C3=A9cessair=
es =C3=A0 ses enfants via les props</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
