<p data-start=3D"4578" data-end=3D"4596" class=3D"">Dans cet exemple :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4597" data-end=3D"4835">
<li data-start=3D"4597" data-end=3D"4689" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4599" data-end=3D"4689" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"459=
9" data-end=3D"4614">BrowserRouter</code> est le conteneur principal qui pe=
rmet de g=C3=A9rer l'historique de navigation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4690" data-end=3D"4753" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4692" data-end=3D"4753" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"469=
2" data-end=3D"4700">Switch</code> est utilis=C3=A9 pour afficher une seule=
 route =C3=A0 la fois.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4754" data-end=3D"4835" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4756" data-end=3D"4835" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"475=
6" data-end=3D"4763">Route</code> est utilis=C3=A9 pour associer un chemin =
(<code data-start=3D"4801" data-end=3D"4807">path</code>) =C3=A0 un composa=
nt =C3=A0 afficher.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4837" data-end=3D"4840" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4842" data-end=3D"4887" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4845" data-end=3D"4887">3. Principaux Concepts de React Router</strong></h2=
>
<h3 data-start=3D"4889" data-end=3D"4932" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4893" data-end=3D"4932">3.1 <code data-start=3D"4899" data-end=3D"4914">Bro=
wserRouter</code> et <code data-start=3D"4918" data-end=3D"4930">HashRouter=
</code></strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"4934" data-end=3D"5255">
<li data-start=3D"4934" data-end=3D"5086" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4936" data-end=3D"5086" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
936" data-end=3D"4955"><code data-start=3D"4938" data-end=3D"4953">BrowserR=
outer</code></strong> : Utilis=C3=A9 pour les applications =C3=A0 pages mul=
tiples (SPA). Il utilise l'historique HTML5, ce qui permet des URLs propres=
 (sans <code data-start=3D"5081" data-end=3D"5084">#</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5090" data-end=3D"5255" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5092" data-end=3D"5255" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
092" data-end=3D"5108"><code data-start=3D"5094" data-end=3D"5106">HashRout=
er</code></strong> : Utilis=C3=A9 pour les applications d=C3=A9ploy=C3=A9es=
 sur des serveurs qui ne g=C3=A8rent pas les routes c=C3=B4t=C3=A9 serveur.=
 Ce type de routage ajoute un <code data-start=3D"5240" data-end=3D"5243">#=
</code> dans l'URL.</p>
</li>
</ul>
